'''Lord Eddard Stark''', also called '''Ned''', is the head of [[House Stark]] and [[Lord of Winterfell]]. He is beheaded on the steps of the [[Great Sept of Baelor]].

==Appearance and Character==
Eddard has a long face and dark hair, and he is grave and quiet. He holds to honour.

==History==
Eddard was the second son of [[Rickard Stark]], born in [[263 AC]]. He was fostered at the [[Eyrie]] with [[Robert I Baratheon|Robert Baratheon]] under [[Jon Arryn]].
In [[282 AC]] his father and brother [[Brandon Stark]] were killed by [[Aerys II Targaryen]], and Eddard joined [[Robert's Rebellion]].
He married [[Catelyn Tully]] at [[Riverrun]]. After the war he returned to [[Winterfell]] with his bastard son, [[Jon Snow]].
In [[289 AC]] he fought in the [[Greyjoy Rebellion]], and afterwards took [[Theon Greyjoy]] as his ward.

==Recent Events==
===A Game of Thrones===
Eddard executes a deserter of the [[Night's Watch]]. [[Robert I Baratheon|King Robert]] comes to Winterfell and names Eddard [[Hand of the King]]. After Robert's death Eddard is arrested and beheaded on the order of [[Joffrey I Baratheon]].

===A Clash of Kings===
His bones are sent north.

